	)
	(text "R30, C30: 1 / (2 pi x 270 x 33 nF) = 17.9 kHz, the low-pass\nof audio.md. GPIO 18 at ALT5 is the PWM pin of the Pi Zero.\nC31 blocks DC. R31 divides first, so RV1 works mid-travel."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 83.82 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "24bf681a-c981-5e65-b0a2-f595f815a83d")
	)
	(text "RV1 is a level ceiling, set once, not a volume knob.\nEXPECTED POSITION: 30 % to 50 % of the travel from\nthe GND end for 2 V peak at the speaker. It depends\non M1's input impedance, 10 to 100 kOhm (to verify\nat bring-up step 18). Software volume: [audio] volume."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "89d91480-cfb2-53d9-8aa7-8d48f92b5079")
	)
	(text "M1 drives the speaker in bridge mode:\nneither SPK_P nor SPK_N is ground.\n8 Ohm speaker only. LS1 is bought and\nsits off the board, wired to J6, the\nboard's connector."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 190.5 86.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7d98db29-f37a-542c-a1b2-03a5c9c722af")
	)
	(text "To verify: M1 pins assumed. Input row 1 VIN, 2 GND, 3 SD,\n4 A+, 5 A-. Output edge 6 OUT+, 7 OUT-. Footprint drawn\nfrom memory: redraw it from the module before ordering.\nPins soldered at both edges carry OUT+ and OUT- to J6.\nA builder may instead wire LS1 to M1's own terminal.\nSD left open: the module pulls it high.\nGain about 24 dB and input impedance: from memory."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 116.84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "99d2fadc-a749-568e-b8c4-d94fd5dff56b")
	)
